	// in the event queue, whichever it is. Where the system makes no such timer it does what Go does: asks for a timer tick of 1 ms
	// (timeBeginPeriod) for as long as the process runs. Where it has the timer but not the packet (Wine), the wait ends by its
	// timeout alone, in whole milliseconds.
